"""
Bilingual domain lexicon for faculty-onboarding questions (post-freeze PF-11).

Each entry maps one or more Arabic surface forms (alternatives separated by ``|``) to the English term the approved
documents use. Forms are written WITHOUT the definite article; ``arabic_text.lookup_forms`` strips articles, clitic
particles and common inflections from the query token before the lookup, so ``للمحاضرين`` finds ``محاضرين``.

Flags:
    q      interrogative or question frame (opens the English question)
    v      verb or verbal noun ("to <verb>" after a stripped ``ل``; "how do I <verb>" after "how")
    h      head noun: directly followed by another noun term it takes "of the" ("phone number OF THE HR Department")
    pl     plural noun: a preceding "what is the" becomes "what are the"
    pt     particle or function word (never counts toward coverage)
    x      dropped from the English query (politeness, copulas); never counts toward coverage
    neg    negation marker (kept; used by the translation check as well)
    {subj} in the English: the next noun term is moved into the slot (Arabic verb-subject order)

Routing vocabulary and document terms only; no policy content, no numbers that answer a question.
"""
